Validation failed for tool "submit_decision":
  - assumptions: must have required properties assumptions

Received arguments:
{
  "case_state": "Paused (void property), on hold waiting for landlord. Two quotes (£1,370.00 and £1,700.00+VAT) are with the landlord. No approval on record. Review 2025-05-09.",
  "next_actions": [
    {
      "type": "REQUEST_INFORMATION",
      "action": "Ask landlord to confirm the reply was about Flat 5, 55 Lantern Quay and give a yes/no on the £1,370 quote",
      "recipient": "Langley, landlord",
      "channel": "email",
      "ledger_id": "A3"
    },
    {
      "type": "WAIT",
      "action": "Hold for landlord, review 2025-05-09",
      "recipient": "internal",
      "channel": "internal",
      "ledger_id": "A1"
    }
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "The request does not approve any quote or assign a contractor",
    "Nothing here settles which quote is chosen, the scope (carpet, tap) or who pays",
    "The landlord's question about the previous refurb invoice is not answered"
  ],
  "remaining_work": [
    "Landlord to confirm property and approve a quote; then record decision and assign contractor (agency, review 2025-05-09)",
    "Check whether the previous refurb invoice was paid (accounts)",
    "Clarify scope: carpet replacement and tap replacement differ from the original request",
    "No tenant messages as property is void"
  ],
  "missing_info": [
    "Landlord approval for this property",
    "Quote documents: provider name mismatch (Eliza Bennett vs Alder Compliance) and Kendall quote not seen",
    "attachment-04 invoice not visible"
  ],
  "outcome": "action_taken",
  "severity": "routine",
  "summary": "The job is paused on a void property while the landlord decides between two quotes. The landlord's last reply named other properties, so it is not approval. I asked on the existing thread which property they meant and for a yes/no on the £1,370 quote, and set a hold with review on 2025-05-09.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "question": "Where does this case stand right now, and what is outstanding?",
      "answer": "On hold for the landlord. Two quotes (£1,370.00 and £1,700.00+VAT) are sent and no valid approval exists, because the landlord's reply and one earlier chase named other properties. Scope questions and the previous invoice query remain open."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the next action, who is it for, and through which channel?",
      "answer": "Email to the landlord (Langley) on the existing thread asking them to confirm the property and say yes or no to the £1,370 quote. Already sent (A3). Hold review 2025-05-09."
    },
    {
      "question": "Does anything need a human decision, and why?",
      "answer": "Not yet. The landlord must decide on the quote. If there is no answer by the review date, chase on a second channel. The previous refurb invoice question may need accounts."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "description": "Put job on hold waiting for landlord, review 2025-05-09"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Added note on conflicts"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "description": "Asked landlord to confirm property and approve quote"
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "first request_information attempt",
      "handling": "Blocked by policy for naming other addresses; resent without them (A3)."
    }
  ],
  "conflicts": [
    "Landlord email and our chase name other properties, not Flat 5, 55 Lantern Quay; not treated as about this job",
    "Quote supplier: email says Eliza Bennett, attached estimate says Alder Compliance",
    "Inspection report dated 5 Jan 2026 but signed 3 Apr 2025",
    "Estimate leaves the carpet and replaces the tap, against the original request"
  ]
}

